---
layout: standalone
title: Lost Souls Phone Check
permalink: /check/
---
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ site.baseUrl }}check/check.css">

<main>
  <header>
    <div class="check-candles" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="check-candle" data-check="camera"></span><span class="check-candle" data-check="storage"></span><span class="check-candle" data-check="browser"></span>
    </div>
    <img class="brand-logo" src="{{ site.baseUrl }}assets/images/door66-logo.svg" alt="Door 66">
    <p class="eyebrow">presents</p>
    <h1 class="site-title">Lost Souls</h1>
    <p class="italic">Three things the spirits must know before you cross the threshold</p>
  </header>

  <section id="phone-check" class="phone-check">
    <p class="check-fallback">This browser can't run the game. Try opening this page in Safari (iPhone) or Chrome (Android). Still stuck? Write to <a href="mailto:inquiries@door66.events">inquiries@door66.events</a> and we'll help.</p>
    <noscript><p>This check needs JavaScript. Turn it on in your browser settings, then reload.</p></noscript>
    <ul class="check-results">
      <li class="check-row" data-check="camera">
        <svg class="check-row-icon"><use href="{{ site.baseUrl }}assets/icons/check-icons.svg#eye"/></svg>
        <span class="check-row-text">
          <span class="check-row-label">Can your eyes pierce the veil?</span>
          <span class="check-row-sub">Camera</span>
          <span class="check-row-error" data-error></span>
        </span>
        <span class="check-row-status"></span>
      </li>
      <li class="check-row" data-check="storage">
        <svg class="check-row-icon"><use href="{{ site.baseUrl }}assets/icons/check-icons.svg#home-heart"/></svg>
        <span class="check-row-text">
          <span class="check-row-label">Will the house remember you?</span>
          <span class="check-row-sub">Saved progress</span>
          <span class="check-row-error" data-error></span>
        </span>
        <span class="check-row-status"></span>
      </li>
      <li class="check-row" data-check="browser">
        <svg class="check-row-icon"><use href="{{ site.baseUrl }}assets/icons/check-icons.svg#user-question"/></svg>
        <span class="check-row-text">
          <span class="check-row-label">Are you truly present?</span>
          <span class="check-row-sub">Browser ready</span>
          <span class="check-row-error" data-error></span>
        </span>
        <span class="check-row-status"></span>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="check-hint">When your phone asks to use the camera, choose <strong>Allow</strong>.</p>
    <button type="button" id="camera-check-btn" class="button" data-check="camera">Begin the ritual</button>

    <div class="check-reveal call-to-action">
      <p class="italic">The veil will part for you</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">You are expected</p>
      <h2 class="site-title">Bembridge House</h2>
      <p>Your character waits at the door.<br>Come when the night is yours.</p>
      <p>Your phone may ask about the camera again at the event. If it does, choose <strong>Allow</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="troubleshooting-section">
      <h3>Troubleshooting Steps</h3>
      <div class="troubleshooting-group" data-check="camera">
        <h4>Camera Issue</h4>
        <ol>
          <li>On iPhone: Settings &gt; Safari &gt; Camera &gt; Allow, then reload this page.</li>
          <li>On Android: tap the lock icon in the address bar &gt; Permissions &gt; Camera &gt; Allow, then reload.</li>
          <li>Open this page directly in Safari (iPhone) or Chrome (Android), not inside an email or social app.</li>
          <li>Close any other app that might be using the camera.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="troubleshooting-group" data-check="storage">
        <h4>Local Storage Issue</h4>
        <ol>
          <li>If you're using Private/Incognito mode, try switching to a regular browsing session.</li>
          <li>Check your browser settings to ensure cookies and site data are allowed.</li>
          <li>Try clearing your browser cache and reloading the page.</li>
          <li>If using Safari, check Settings &gt; Safari &gt; Block All Cookies and ensure it's disabled.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="troubleshooting-group" data-check="browser">
        <h4>Browser Compatibility Issue</h4>
        <ol>
          <li>Update your browser to the latest version.</li>
          <li>If you're using an older device, try a different browser (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, or Edge).</li>
          <li>Check if your browser has any extensions that might be blocking features.</li>
          <li>Try disabling browser extensions temporarily to see if that resolves the issue.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="contact-section">
        <h4>Still Having Issues?</h4>
        <p>If these steps don't resolve the problem, please contact us for assistance. Include details about which checks failed and what device/browser you're using.</p>
        <p><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:inquiries@door66.events">inquiries@door66.events</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<script>
  // Plain old JavaScript on purpose: this has to run in browsers too old for the check script,
  // so it tests for the newest feature that script needs (async functions).
  try {
    new Function('async () => {}');
  } catch (e) {
    document.getElementById('phone-check').setAttribute('data-state', 'unsupported');
  }
</script>

<script src="{{ site.baseUrl }}js/phone-check.js" defer></script>
